  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/93B70E">Proposition <span data-tag="93B70E">5.5.9.1</span> <span class="named">(Quillen)</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a category which admits finite products, and let $\mathbf{A}$ denote the category of functors $F: \calC \rightarrow \sSet $ which preserve finite products. Then $\mathbf{A}$ has the structure of a simplicial model category, where: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(W)$"><p>
A natural transformation $\alpha : F \rightarrow F'$ of functors is a weak equivalence in $\mathbf{A}$ if and only if $\alpha (C): F(C) \rightarrow F'(C)$ is a weak homotopy equivalence of simplicial sets, for every $C \in \calC $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(F)$"><p>
A natural transformation $\alpha : F \rightarrow F'$ of functors is a fibration in $\mathbf{A}$ if and only if $\alpha (C): F(C) \rightarrow F'(C)$ is a Kan fibration of simplicial sets, for every $C \in \calC $. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
